  "official_listing": "https://www.olimpiadadematematica.cl/",
  "scope": "All 46 senior problems in the 12 published IMO and Iberoamerican selection papers: Ibero 2013–2015, shared IMO/Ibero 2016, IMO 2022–2026, Ibero 2023–2025. No claim for absent years. Cono Sur-only tests and practice sheets excluded. Original problem 1 of Ibero 2024 and IMO 2025 is excluded because the paper explicitly assigns it only to Cono Sur. Continuous bank numbering; original numbers retained in source evidence. Day 1 means IMO and day 2 means Ibero in 2023–2025; day omitted in single-paper years. The 2016 shared paper is stored once.",
  "review": "Every statement page and formula visually compared; all subparts and four source figures included. The scanned handwritten IMO 2024 paper was read visually. All linked downloads contain statements only. The 2026 download is a raster-only assembly of the four official statement excerpts; solution pixels and original PDF objects are absent. The underlying original 2026 source contains solutions and is labelled accordingly.",
  "source_domain_notes": {
    "cl.2013.0.1": "Source domain note: the official paper asks for integer solutions but does not specify a convention for 0^0. The printed domain is preserved; no additional convention is assumed.",
    "cl.2023.2.6": "Source domain note: the official paper does not specify the domain of the parameter c. This omission is preserved rather than silently imposing an integer or real domain.",
    "cl.2024.1.2": "Editorial domain clarification: m ≥ 2 and k ≥ 1. The handwritten original gives m, k as natural numbers without excluding m = 1, which would make the divisibility assertion involve a zero divisor.",
    "cl.2025.2.7": "Editorial domain clarification: the equation is required for x in R excluding 0 and 1, matching the declared domain of f. The official paper instead prints “for every x in R”, where the expressions are undefined at those two points."
  },
  "gaps": "No senior selection paper retrieved for 2017–2021; no Ibero paper for 2022 or 2026 is listed. The national final archive is separate and not imported in this selection-test collection. As of 2026-10-03, the 2026 national final is scheduled for 22–24 October.",
